{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he will save them, like his people the flock</b> — by the hand of Moses when he stood at the sea, as it says: \"You led like a flock your people by the hand of Moses\" etc. And because he mentioned sling-stones, he said that these Hasmoneans are crown-stones of diadem and glory." "<b>Skipping about</b> — that they are seen as a nest upon the land of HaShem. It is also fitting for them to be stones, hinting that they are high priests."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase 'like his people the flock' alludes to Psalm 77:21; Ibn Ezra's Hebrew weaves the verse into his syntax rather than marking it as a formal citation.", 1 "The word כנס could mean 'nest' or be a form of כינוס ('gathering'); translated hyper-literally as 'nest' per its primary sense, though the image of stones in a nest is unusual and the reading may be textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:37.433218720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}